# Shared secret guarding both endpoints, sent as the `x-scraper-secret` header.
#
# Without it this service is an open scraping proxy on your Vercel bandwidth,
# so it is required — src/auth.ts rejects every request when it is unset.
#
# Generate:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('hex'))"
#
# The same value must be set in three places, or the collectors fail with a
# silent 401: here (or the Vercel project's env vars), and the `Set Config`
# node of each workflow in ../../n8n.
SCRAPER_SECRET=

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Lets /api/enrich resolve a company's website when no source named one.
#
# Optional by design. Wuzzuf hands over `website` and `linkedinProfile` for
# every company, a schema.org JobPosting often carries `hiringOrganization
# .sameAs`, and an ATS apply URL is frequently the company's own domain — so
# most companies resolve with no search at all. This only covers the rest.
#
# It is an API key rather than a scraper because the obvious shortcut is not
# available: DuckDuckGo's robots.txt disallows both /lite and /html, and Google
# and Bing disallow their result pages outright. Brave has a free tier.
# https://brave.com/search/api/
BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=
